<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2>What operators ask about the record.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>How does survey cadence change what we report?</summary>
        <div><p>A leak counts from the last survey to the day it was found, or the whole year after a single survey. More documented surveys, shorter windows.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Federal rules in one state, a stricter program in another. Two systems?</summary>
        <div><p>No. Intervals, repair loops, and required fields vary by facility and program inside one record set.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Federal rules are in flux. Why tighten the program now?</summary>
        <div><p>States and buyers did not move with them. Both still ask for a verifiable record at the component.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does the EU Methane Regulation reach us through European buyers?</summary>
        <div><p>Yes. EU importers need MRV equivalent to the EU's own, such as OGMP 2.0 Level 5, which is built from component records. That is the record Assetas keeps.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can we bring our existing history in?</summary>
        <div><p>Yes. Bring an export of your leak log and we will show you what maps directly.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How does the assistant handle a regulatory question?</summary>
        <div><p>It works on your records and the regulatory text, and shows what it read.</p></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

